mulative distribution function is\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{x}}{2},\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ h(x),\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}."] [17592186503695 "Compute $P(-1<X<1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{28}({x}^{2}+1),\\, & -2\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186504601 "The function $h(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nh(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{x+a}-\\sqrt{2+a}}, & x\\ne 2, \\\\ 6, & x=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=2,$ what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$ {{field-1}}"] [17592186504603 "The function $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡(2x+k), & x\\ne -1, \\\\ 3, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1,$ what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186504606 "The function $g(x)$ is given by \n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-\\sqrt{1-x}}{ax}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor what value of $a$ is the function continuous at $x=0?$"] [17592186504607 "The function $g(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x-b}-\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-b}}, & x\\ne 0, \\\\ 10, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor what value of $b$ is the function continuous at $x=0?$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186504608 "Find the $72.9$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{16}\\sqrt{x},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186504611 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{cx+4}, & x\\ne -1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{27}, & x=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1,$ what is the value of $c?$"] [17592186504614 "The function $f(x)$ defined by \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\b